@startuml
title ILM platform - local Docker Compose deployment

left to right direction
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false

actor "Operator" as operator
node "Web browser" as browser {
  artifact "Administrator UI\n(SPA)" as ui
}

node "Docker host\n127.0.0.1:8000" as dockerHost {
  node "Docker Compose network: ilm-local_default" as compose {
    component "Kong gateway\n:8000" as kong
    component "Core\nSpring Boot :8080" as core
    component "Auth\nASP.NET :8080" as auth
    component "OPA\n:8181" as opa
    component "OPA policy bundle server\nNginx :8080" as policies
    component "Scheduler\nSpring Boot :8080" as scheduler
    component "Keycloak\nHTTP :8080, HTTPS :8443" as keycloak
    component "Administrator frontend\nNginx :8080" as frontend
    queue "RabbitMQ\nAMQP :5672" as rabbit
    database "PostgreSQL :5432\ncore / keycloak data" as postgres

    component "Register OIDC\n(one-shot init job)" as register
    component "Generate admin certificate\n(one-shot init job)" as certificate
  }

  folder "Generated local files" as generated {
    artifact "Realm import\nRabbitMQ definitions\nAdmin certificate" as configFiles
  }
}

operator --> browser
browser --> kong : HTTP
note on link
  Published only on host loopback:
  http://localhost:8000
end note

kong --> frontend : /administrator/**
kong --> core : /api/**\n/login, /logout
kong --> keycloak : /kc/**

core --> postgres : JDBC
auth --> postgres : SQL
keycloak --> postgres : JDBC
scheduler --> postgres : JDBC

core --> auth : HTTP :8080\nusers, roles, permissions
core --> opa : HTTP :8181\npolicy decisions
opa --> policies : HTTP :8080\nfetch policy bundle
core --> scheduler : HTTP :8080\nscheduled jobs
core --> rabbit : AMQP :5672\nplatform events / jobs
scheduler --> rabbit : AMQP :5672\nscheduled work

register --> core : HTTP :8080\ncreate local admin\nregister OIDC provider
register --> keycloak : HTTP :8080\ncheck realm discovery
certificate --> configFiles : write generated certificate
keycloak --> configFiles : import realm
rabbit --> configFiles : load definitions
register --> configFiles : read certificate

note right of kong
  Reverse-proxy routes
  /administrator -> frontend
  /api            -> Core
  /login, /logout -> Core
  /kc             -> Keycloak
end note

note right of core
  Core API groups
  - REST management: certificate and cryptographic asset inventories
  - Profiles: RA, token, compliance, ACME, SCEP, CMP, TSP
  - Connectors, discovery, workflows and scheduled jobs
  - Settings, users/roles, audit, notifications and dashboard
  - ACME, SCEP and CMP client protocols
  - Liveness/readiness: /api/v1/health/*
end note

note right of auth
  Auth API groups
  - Users, roles and permissions
  - Health: /health
end note

note right of opa
  OPA API groups
  - Authorization decisions: /v1/data/*
  - Health and bundle readiness: /health?bundles
end note

note right of policies
  Policy bundle HTTP endpoint
  GET /bundles/bundle.tar.gz
end note

note right of scheduler
  Scheduler API groups
  - Job scheduling / management
  - Health: /health
end note

note right of keycloak
  Identity and access APIs
  - OIDC discovery, login, token and logout
  - Keycloak administration
  - Publicly routed under /kc
end note

note right of rabbit
  Messaging API
  - AMQP queues and exchanges
  - Used internally by Core and Scheduler
end note

note bottom of postgres
  Shared local database service.
  Core, Auth and Scheduler use application data;
  Keycloak uses the keycloak schema.
end note

legend bottom
  Deployment represents the development stack in test-ilm/compose.yaml.
  Connectors and external certificate authorities / timestamp providers
  are integration targets, not deployed by this Compose stack.
endlegend
@enduml
